  "id": "ticket_01KYAY563XSEE9C0AEZ7MH23HG",
  "name": "Rewrite slop web as a React + Tailwind + shadcn/ui SPA, bundled offline into the binary",
  "slug": "rewrite-slop-web-as-a",
  "spec": {
    "summary": "Replace the server-rendered HTML web UI with a real shadcn/ui SPA (user-chosen direction)",
    "details_md": "Rewrite `slop web`'s frontend as a React + Tailwind + shadcn/ui single-page app, generated with the shadcn CLI, served by the existing Bun.serve over a NEW read-only JSON API built on the current data-source layer. The whole SPA (JS/CSS/fonts) must be bundled into the `slop` binary so it still runs fully offline, same-origin, with NO CDN or external fetch — preserving the strict no-external-request posture. This re-opens a read-only \"web v2\" (distinct from F9's mutation scope: still read-only). Must carry forward ALL the wave-1 web security/robustness fixes into the new server wiring: Host-header allowlist (DNS-rebinding), jira URL scheme safety, config.yaml fault-tolerance (warn not 500), HEAD support, reusePort:false. Dark mode required. Keep feature parity with every current view.",
    "acceptance": [
      "slop web serves a React+Tailwind+shadcn SPA; all assets bundled into the binary; zero external/CDN requests (offline works)",
      "Read-only preserved: SPA only GETs; server exposes a read-only JSON API over the existing WebDataSource",
      "Feature parity: ticket list+filters, tree (jira badges), ticket detail (spec/timeline/sessions/plans), transcript viewer, review panel, stale panel",
      "Wave-1 web fixes carried forward: Host allowlist, safe jira URL, config fault-tolerance, HEAD, reusePort:false",
      "bun run build still emits the single self-contained binary with the SPA embedded; server + API have tests; a build-artifact smoke test passes"
    ],
    "context": [
      "src/web/ (server.ts, data-source.ts, views/*, assets/*)",
